{"chunk_id": "0cca2eb25291", "text": "The insulted Valakhilya sages, enraged by Indra\u2019s arrogance, begin a powerful sacrifice intended to create another Indra capable of rivaling the king of the gods. Alarmed, Indra seeks refuge with the sage Kasyapa, who persuades the ascetics not to contradict Brahma\u2019s decree that Indra rule the three worlds. Instead, their sacrifice will produce a mighty lord of birds. Through Kasyapa and Vinata are born Aruna, the charioteer of the Sun, and Garuda, destined to rule all winged beings. The narrative then shifts to Garuda\u2019s immense power: he assaults the gods guarding the nectar of immortality (amrita), darkening the heavens with the storm of his wings and battling the celestials in a terrifying display of strength.\nGaruda attacks the gods to seize the guarded Soma, scattering and wounding them with the storm of his wings.\nThemes: divine conflict, Garuda's power, quest for amrita, cosmic battle", "vector": [0.015243236906826496, -0.02215476706624031, -0.003939301241189241, -0.0001157064107246697, -0.00858192890882492, 0.020531706511974335, -0.04071174934506416, -0.013877160847187042, -0.002221563132479787, -0.019138580188155174, 0.010455209761857986, 0.01467516552656889, 0.004057649523019791, -0.010313192382454872, 0.005281707271933556, -0.0019967015832662582, 0.03960265964269638, -0.0034574554301798344, 0.017434367910027504, -0.00330360303632915, -0.012619289569556713, 0.01896274834871292, -0.018178269267082214, 0.027943680062890053, -0.0010110309813171625, 0.021735476329922676, 0.0013153547188267112, -0.01970665156841278, 0.017488468438386917, -0.015797782689332962, -0.00856840331107378, -0.004754212684929371, -0.0019527438562363386, 0.01436407957226038, -0.025590242817997932, -0.012761307880282402, -0.007925941608846188, -0.006985920015722513, 0.009494899772107601, 0.008358757942914963, 0.008832150138914585, -0.0060120839625597, 0.007195564918220043, 0.011043569073081017, -0.006133813410997391, 0.015473170205950